sn5.2:2.1 starts: “That state so hard to achieve
sn5.2:2.2 starts: Which is to be attained by the seers,
sn5.2:2.3 starts: Can’t be attained by a woman
sn5.2:2.4 starts: With her two-fingered wisdom.”
sn5.3:2.1 starts: “Why now, when your son is dead,
sn5.3:2.2 starts: Do you sit alone with tearful face?
sn5.3:2.3 starts: Having entered the woods all alone,
sn5.3:2.4 starts: Are you on the lookout for a man?”
sn5.4:5.1 starts: “I am repelled and humiliated
sn5.4:5.2 starts: By this foul, putrid body,
sn5.4:5.3 starts: Subject to break up, fragile:
sn5.4:5.4 starts: I’ve uprooted sensual craving.
